    "body": "Pattern to copy (read from `wcs_page.rs` on main, against `pages.rs` / `setup_pages.rs`). What the WCS page does that Stock, Machine, Fixtures, Tool list and Setup do not:\n\n1. **Named groups.** Content sits in titled, collapsible `layout::group` sections (\"Origin and orientation\", \"Quarter turns\", \"Anchor on\"). The five pages are one flat run of controls, split by bare `ui.separator()` or nothing.\n2. **Label-left grid.** Fields are rows of `prop_grid` (label column fixed at `LABEL_W`, control beside it, all controls in one column). Stock uses the stacked \"caption over control\" `field()`+`num()` pair; Machine's Library row is a bare `horizontal`; Setup, Tool list and Fixtures print values as space-padded text lines (`\"    stock ..., WCS placed\"`, `\"    {tool}  2 ops  1 change ...\"`).\n3. **Equal-width action rows.** Actions are `even_row` buttons filling the pane width, at a fixed height, placed once under the content they act on. The five use natural-width buttons in `horizontal` / `horizontal_wrapped` rows, small buttons pushed right per row (Setups), and conditional extra buttons that make the row jump.\n4. **Progressive disclosure.** Only the controls for the current choice are drawn (the \"Anchor on\" choice swaps the compass for the circle picker). Stock draws everything at once (all fit margins, the size fields and the source rows); Fixtures and Machine show every secondary action all the time.\n5. **One quiet helper line, not paragraphs.** A short `small().weak()` line under a group heading says what a group does (\"About the world axes; applied at once.\"). The five use full-size sentences, or hover-less prose such as the long Setups footer.\n6. **Plain-English labels** with the technical word in brackets (\"Tilt about X (roll)\"). Several of the five use bare labels or run-together strings (\"Per side\", \"Fit margin -X\", raw \"Machine\" heading).\n7. **A readout at the foot** (what is placed now) instead of making the user infer state from the fields.\n\nPlan: one PR per page, Stock first (own module `stock_page.rs`, which also takes `pages.rs` further under the 400-line law). Each PR keeps the existing commands and carries before/after screenshots. Open PRs checked first: #773, #1209, #1124 (none touches the Stock page body; #1209 and #1124 edit `pages.rs` elsewhere).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
